        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-08T00:30:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are the semantics here any more complicated than simply \"the new output mark overrides the old output mark\"? For example, is zero treated specially? Can zero be used to clear the existing mark?\n\nIt seems like that would be dangerous/incorrect unless the code can distinguish \"application did not pass in an XFRMA_OUTPUT_MARK attribute\" from \"application passed in an XFRMA_OUTPUT_MARK attribute and its value was zero. As far as I can tell the code can\u0027t do that.\n\nRegardless, this should be explained here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "941e82e9f85ba13b2d13312fa7766a704e4f6a1c",
